From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:06:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sb/intel/lynxpoint: Fix xHCI MaxPorts field programming

MaxPorts is HCSPARAMS1[31:24], and LPT-H needs 15 + the number of
SuperSpeed ports in it, i.e. 21 (0x15). The native USB init however
masks and shifts the value by 28 bits: only bits 31:28 get cleared, and
21 << 28 truncates to 5 << 28. If the field is writable and starts out
as 0x15, MaxPorts reads back as 0x55 (85) afterwards, so the OS and
payloads see 64 extra root hub ports that do not exist.

Program the whole 8-bit field.

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541. Not tested on hardware yet: HCSPARAMS1, e.g.
in /sys/kernel/debug/usb/xhci/0000:00:14.0/reg-cap, must report 0x15
in bits 31:24.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
index cb6f6ee8e..b63ae3d50 100644
--- a/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
+++ b/src/southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/early_usb_native.c
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ static void common_xhci_hc_init(void)
 
 	if (!is_lp) {
 		const unsigned int max_ports = 15 + ss_port_count();
-		clrsetbits32(xhci_bar + XHCI_HCS_PARAMS_1, 0xf << 28, max_ports << 28);
+		clrsetbits32(xhci_bar + XHCI_HCS_PARAMS_1, 0xffU << 24, max_ports << 24);
 	}
 
 	clrsetbits32(xhci_bar + XHCI_HCS_PARAMS_3, 0xffff << 16 | 0xff, 0x200 << 16 | 0x0a);
